{"availability":"available","full":"Aurtechmx/openlidarviewer","name":"openlidarviewer","description":"Browser-based LiDAR and point-cloud viewer - measure, classify, profile, and export, entirely client-side on WebGPU with a WebGL2 fallback. Runs locally, no upload.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":24,"forks":4,"created":"2026-06-03T05:31:11Z","updated":"2026-10-11T00:07:55Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lidar.aurtech.mx/","topics":["3d-spatial","3d-visualization","copc","drone-lidar","geospatial","gis","lidar","lidar-data","point-cloud","point-cloud-viewer","remote-sensing","research-development","research-tool","spatial-computing","surveying","threejs","webgl","webgpu"],"demo":"https://app.openlidarviewer.org/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T00:22:54.200Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T00:22:54.200Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T00:22:54.200Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:41.171Z","stars":23,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:42:54.562Z","stars":23,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:02:57.590Z","stars":23,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-11T00:22:54.200Z","stars":24,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser-native LiDAR and point-cloud viewer for fast local inspection, 3D navigation, measurement, and terrain analysis. Local-first, cited, honest about what it can't tell you.","OpenLiDARViewer opens LiDAR and point-cloud datasets straight in the browser. You inspect a scan, navigate it in 3D, change how it is coloured, measure, run terrain analysis and export the results, with no desktop GIS to set up. Files are read and rendered locally, so there is no server to upload to.","It is a viewer and an inspection tool, not a GIS or a survey-grade processing suite. Every result states its coverage, its method and its uncertainty, and a terrain or contour export is gated on evidence rather than produced on request."],"features":["Inspect point-cloud datasets in a modern web interface, with nothing to install and nothing uploaded.","Stream large COPC and EPT datasets progressively, octree node by octree node, with bounded memory and no full-file load.","Navigate game-style: Orbit, Walk, Fly, and Pan modes with WASD and mouse-look, plus Top / Iso / Oblique / Planar camera presets.","Measure distance, polyline, area, height, angle, slope, cross-section profile, and volume cut/fill, with editable points and JSON session export/import.","Switch themes (Dark / Light / High-contrast), drive everything from a command palette (Cmd-K), and work one-handed on mobile."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aurtechmx/openlidarviewer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"85a901d95e90068f824c3756168889f91c37b6e4990777c8c296348e5d4e7284","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:50:51.265Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:22.881Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A browser-native LiDAR and point-cloud viewer for fast local inspection, 3D navigation, measurement, and terrain analysis. Local-first, cited, honest about what it can't tell you.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aurtechmx/openlidarviewer/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No install, no account, no upload.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aurtechmx/openlidarviewer/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Some formats may require a paid plan.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aurtechmx/openlidarviewer/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"85a901d95e90068f824c3756168889f91c37b6e4990777c8c296348e5d4e7284","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aurtechmx/openlidarviewer/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:22.882Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T11:59:42Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aurtechmx/openlidarviewer/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:22.884Z","hash":"85a901d95e9006